{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 4f439a6d and a91ddbc9: repair the lineage now, deploy main, then continue J4 on the new source. This replaces item 3 of f71e8a29 (no deployment until the J4 witness closes).\n\nWhat I confirmed by reading the source at 5dc9765f. This is a source reading, not an observed run.\n- register.ts sends create-directory from the selected confirmed outcome entry, and names the found entry in fields.claim.\n- workspace-lineage.ts:53-56 reads the Directory genesis source as the claim and requires an act of kind found. At :75 it requires fields.claim to equal that source. A real room has two different facts here, so workspaceRepository returns null.\n- workspace-host.ts:182 returns null when the lineage is null, and operations.ts then records unknown with basis none.\nSo on a room created through the real Register, every head operation ends unknown without reaching the provider. That fits both S1 attempts and the empty telemetry. No record shows it directly, so write \"consistent with\", and the diagnosis must confirm it on the next attempt. V14 setup reaches this path at hold-a, so withdrawing it was right.\n\n1. V14 stays unused. Its admission and finisher stay as history. Do not run setup on the current Worker.\n\n2. Repair in the same head as head diagnosis 4f3336c1. This ruling amends that request's scope, so there is one head and one gate. The repair:\n- Read the Directory genesis source as the selected confirmed create-repository outcome, and verify the send from it.\n- Bind that outcome to its operation, and that operation's opening to the found act named in fields.claim. Keep the found act and seed-effect checks, against the found entry.\n- Keep every other predicate. Raise the read bound only by the one read that the extra fact needs, and say so.\n- Audit the other readers of this lineage and any test that scripts the same shape. Report what you find.\n\n3. The witness must use the real shape: build the lineage through the actual Register rules, not a scripted found sender. It fails on the old predicate and passes on the new one. Add a forged-claim case and an unselected-outcome case, both refused. The checker reviews this as an authority predicate.\n\n4. Update plan 034's status: the recovery reader is not scheduled, and its premise waits on what the next attempt shows.\n\n5. Order: this head first, after the current S4 Native run ends. S4 then continues.\n\n6. Deployment: after landing, I deploy main to dap-demo, dap-grow and dap-lending, with BO1, DX-A2 and S3. I will report the destination@16 change. The deployment changes the J4 witness's pinned Worker version, and the witness report must say so.\n\n7. J4: prepare a successor packet bound to the new source and Worker version. It keeps the scratch room, the published policy, both enrolled agents and all originals. Check that the room still reads under the new Worker before setup.\n\n8. S1: after J4's setup closes, one third scratch room may run under the approved runbook on the deployed repair. Both stopped rooms stay stopped. If its head still ends unknown, stop and report the diagnosis.\n\nAlso accepted: the metric-dropped rows are terminal summaries with zero loss counters (f6e9213b), so the concern in 3ed61daa falls away.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4f3336c17fe8c0e3b3065b272f0b7c101850ca38 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:364be032963705e2746eb41a8fd37b232d456fb4, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4aa3a00525fb9f500e2c9640ccab369106838cf1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:96416841dead2e1a55f7797fae0ea7c6e8ea8c8c and 2 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}